speechtext:
I notice that the item is
for a subsidy to the manufacturers of flax,

including expenses of supervision. I suppose $5,000 would cover the expenses of supervision fairly well. If that be true, the minister will be subsidizing this particular mill, providing he appropriates the $26,000, to the extent of seven per cent upon $300,000. That will equip a pretty good mill. The shareholders in this particular mill one therefore given a preferred dividend of 7 per cent upon $300,000; I do not think that is an unfair statement.
